1. Why Roles are Important in Real Projects

Imagine a company has 50 servers.

They may need:

Apache
Nginx
Docker
Monitoring Agent
Users
Security Configuration

Instead of creating one huge playbook, we can create separate roles:

roles/
├── apache/
├── nginx/
├── docker/
├── monitoring/
├── users/
└── security/

This makes automation much easier to manage.

2. Role Reusability

One of the biggest advantages of roles is reusability.

Suppose you create an apache role.

You can use the same role in:

Development
Testing
Production

You don't need to rewrite all Apache tasks again.

             ┌── Development
Apache Role ─┼── Testing
             └── Production
